        "source": "inherited",
        "where": "inferred policy",
        "note": "Not an explicit statement of physical opening days: it is the policy that reproduces all fifteen monthly rows of the report. Weekend holidays are not deducted twice."
      },
      {
        "area": "November 2026 and November 2027",
        "value": "40 half-days at 100 % (20 at 50 %)",
        "source": "correction",
        "where": "PDF p.1",
        "note": "Both rows literally read «40 journées». Read as 40 DEMI-journées, inferred from every other row and from the 2:1 relation between the two subscription levels. 40 whole days would be 80 half-days and is NOT granted. Confirm with the association before #1600 publishes."
      },
      {
        "area": "Level labels",
        "value": "Étage 1 · Étage 2 (singleRoomLevelNames on)",
        "source": "explicit",
        "where": "PDF p.2"
      },
      {
        "area": "Legend",
        "value": "booking_rules.legend_profile «simple»",
        "source": "explicit",
        "where": "PDF p.3",
        "note": "Four entries: Place libre · Place réservée · Ma place · Place non disponible."
      },
      {
        "area": "Visible vocabulary",
        "value": "Place · Étage · Réservations · Place libre · Place réservée · Ma place · Place non disponible",
        "source": "explicit",
        "where": "PDF pp.2–4",
        "note": "legendUnavailable became an overridable key with #1597."
      },
      {
        "area": "Whole-table reservations on Étage 2",
        "value": "each Étage 2 table bookable_as_whole false · individual places still bookable",
        "source": "unresolved",
        "where": "PDF p.3",
        "note": "The demand is per DESK, and a level flag alone does not fulfil it: the rehearsal refuses the Étage 2 table with «desk not bookable as a whole» while the Étage 2 LEVEL flag refuses separately and a place on the same table still books. No table exists in this template to carry the flag, because the inventory below is unresolved; #1600 sets it on each real Étage 2 table once the inventory is relevé. «Journée entière» is a time period and is not touched. Étage 1 keeps whole-table booking."
      },
      {
        "area": "Physical inventory",
        "value": "two levels, no tables, no places",
        "source": "unresolved",
        "where": "PDF p.3",
        "note": "The floor-plan crops show Table 1 and places 21/22 only; that establishes neither a table count nor a 22-place space. The generic eight-seat example is deliberately NOT carried: it is not Pézenas inventory. Obtain the verified layout before #1600."
      },
      {
        "area": "Navigation",
        "value": "combined Calendar destination · events tab off · members directory off · member account menu on",
        "source": "explicit",
        "where": "PDF p.4",
        "note": "calendarHub, calendarViews and calendarValidations on; eventsTab, membersDirectory and memberPage off; memberAccountMenu from #1598 keeps the account controls without Réglages."
      },
      {
        "area": "Bureau roles",
        "value": "Trésorier·ère · Secrétaire · Référent·e de salle, defined and unassigned",
        "source": "inherited",
        "where": "association_fr",
        "note": "Definitions only. Applying grants nothing until an owner gives a role to somebody; no officer is invented."
      },
      {
        "area": "VAT regime",
        "value": "not_subject",
        "source": "inherited",
        "where": "association_fr",
        "note": "An inherited association default, NOT a verified tax status for Pézenas."
      },
      {
        "area": "Whole-space booking at all (levelBooking)",
        "value": "off",
        "source": "inherited",
        "where": "core default",
        "note": "With it off — which is what applying this template leaves — NO whole level, room or table can be booked anywhere, so the Étage 2 demand is already met a fortiori and Étage 1 loses nothing the report gave it. The per-table flag above is what keeps the demand true if Pézenas ever switches whole-space booking on. The rehearsal proves both states."
      },
      {
        "area": "Booking horizon and quota protections",
        "value": "advance_horizon_days 90 · max_series_days 180 · quota and overage rules unchanged",
        "source": "inherited",
        "where": "association_fr",
        "note": "The report imposes neither a horizon nor a one-half-day-per-day limit, so the existing defaults stand."
      },
